// sqlite: embedded SQLite, with an API close to better-sqlite3 (README.md). The driver is the
// package's native library (native/, Rust over rusqlite, SQLite compiled in); `sqlite/engine` is
// a SQLite engine written in Velt (read-only for now; docs/engine.md).
//
// Synchronous by design: a typical query takes microseconds, less than handing it to a
// blocking thread pool and back would cost, and SQLite serializes writers anyway. Run a long
// query in `spawn(...)` to keep it off the current task.
//
// Parameters bind as their JSON text would: an object binds by name (`:id`, `@id`, `$id` all
// take the field `id`), an array (or a single number or string) binds `?` by position. int →
// INTEGER, float → REAL, string → TEXT, bool → 0/1, null → NULL, `u8[]` → BLOB. Rows are decoded
// by velt/db's `decodeRows` from the library's row cursor: each column fills the field of the
// same name (rename with `AS`). INTEGER decodes into integer fields exactly (all of i64) and into
// `f64` fields; REAL into `f64`; TEXT into `string`; BLOB into `u8[]`; NULL into `T | null`
// fields. SQLite has no booleans: a column declared `BOOLEAN` decodes into `bool`, any other 0/1
// value (an expression) needs an integer field.

export { Database, open, OpenOptions } from "./database";
export { SqliteError } from "./errors";
export { RunResult } from "./run_result";
export { Statement } from "./statement";
export { Transaction } from "./transaction";
